this is the list of files in linc.cis.upenn.edu  pub/NH3.0/mac:
-rw-r--r--  1 222      50           1639 May 16 03:36 README.mac
-rw-r--r--  1 222      50         486017 May 15 02:34 nh30j+.hqx
-rw-r--r--  1 222      50           8024 May 15 02:34 nh30j.doc
-rw-r--r--  1 222      50         485866 May 15 02:35 nh30j.hqx
-rw-r--r--  1 222      50         115267 May 15 02:35 playground.hqx

README.mac describes nh30j.doc as an owners manual.  it also says
that you need playground.hqx (binhex encoded, self-extracting archive)
to create the playground where you'll eventually install one of the
two games nh30j.hqx or nh30j+.hqx.  nh30j.hqx is the default choice
for the game, however it doesn't work in some environments (i.e.
on some mac IIfx's a/o under system 7.0).  for the cases where
nh30j.hqx doesn't work, nh30j+.hqx should work but the price you
pay is the required 3MB MultiFinder partition (i.e. it has minimal
memory management).

when you get it up and running, let us know how it is.  thanx,

